details.contract:
`binary_smoke.rs` uses `env!("CARGO_BIN_EXE_sangkar")` and:
- runs `<bin> status --repo-root <fixture>` with `PATH` set to an empty directory and `HOME` to a temp dir, asserting exit 0 — a binary that shells out to an interpreter fails here;
- runs `<bin> index` on the `polyglot` fixture with the same stripped environment, asserting exit 0 and that `<dataDir>/graph.db` exists;
- runs all seven tools against that database and asserts each exits 0 with a status other than error;
- runs `<bin> mcp` with the recorded `rust/tests/vectors/mcp_session.ndjson` on stdin and asserts the response lines parse as JSON and carry no `Content-Length` header;
- asserts the binary has no sibling `.wasm`/`.node`/`node_modules` requirement (check the binary's directory listing).
Keep the runtime under 60 s; no network, no host state. The release target is Linux x64, so no cross-platform skip is needed — but if the test ever runs elsewhere, skip the empty-`PATH` variant with an explicit message rather than a false pass.
